BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (Lognormal regression on order statistics \(ROS\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(Take the natural log of every detected concentration. Sort all observations \(detects and) Tj T*
(censored limits\) in joint ascending order by converted concentration. A censored limit ranks) Tj T*
(below a detect reported at the same numeric value, because the true concentration is at or) Tj T*
(below the limit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assign each rank i = 1..n the Cunnane plotting position p = \(i - 0.4\) / \(n + 0.2\) and the) Tj T*
(standard normal quantile z of p. Regress the log-detects on their normal quantiles \(ordinary) Tj T*
(least squares\): the fitted line gives the lognormal location and scale. The regression uses) Tj T*
(detects only; censored limits are never regressed, only imputed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Impute each censored observation from the fitted line at its own rank quantile. The) Tj T*
(completed log-sample is the observed log-detects plus the imputed values. Its mean mu and) Tj T*
(sample standard deviation sigma \(denominator n - 1\) are the lognormal parameters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The 90th percentile estimate is p90 = exp\(mu + z_0.90 * sigma\), where z_0.90 is the 0.90) Tj T*
(quantile of the standard normal. Report p90 in mg/L rounded half up to four decimals.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
